<$TOP/mkfiles/mkfile.proto

# the goken cross-toolchain itself: used by tests/ (mk objtype=386) and,
# once self-hosting is viable, as CC/AS/LD for the top-level build too
O=8
CC=8c
LD=8l
AS=8a
AR=iar

# -Dcputype386 (word-shaped, not lib_core/libc/mkfile's usual bare
# -D$cputype): "386" alone is a valid #define name (Xc's cpp accepts
# `-D386`) but NOT a valid #ifdef *operand* -- purely numeric tokens
# fail there ("syntax in #if(n)def"), confirmed empirically (this
# compiler has no other arch whose $cputype is a bare number, so
# nothing else in this tree has ever hit it). port/getcallerpc.c's own
# #ifdef needs to tell this arch apart from the others, hence this
# word-shaped alias, set here (arch-specific) rather than in
# lib_core/libc/mkfile (which would have to special-case 386 in a
# supposedly-generic, every-arch code path).
CFLAGS=$CFLAGS_COMMON -I$TOP/include/arch/386 -Dcputype386

# lib_core/libc/port/getcallerpc.c's own #ifdef guards out its portable
# fallback for this arch, expecting a real implementation instead --
# see lib_core/libc/arch/386/getcallerpc.s and lib_core/libc/mkfile's
# own ARCHEXTRAOFILES comment for why this is set here, not there.
ARCHEXTRAOFILES=arch/386/getcallerpc.$O
